@startuml
title RuleSphere - Submit, Review and Build\nUC-10..14
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #177E8D
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBackgroundColor #EAF6F8

actor "Decision Author" as Author
actor "Authorized Reviewer(s)" as Reviewer
boundary "Management API" as API
participant AuthorizationService as Auth
participant Release
participant DecisionValidator as Validator
participant GovernancePolicy as Policy
database "Approval / Audit Evidence" as Evidence
participant ArtifactBuilder as Builder
database "Artifact Store" as Artifacts

Author -> API: Submit candidate revision
activate API

API -> Auth: authorize(author, submit, scope)
activate Auth
Auth --> API: Access decision
deactivate Auth

break Unauthorized submit
  API --> Author: Access denied
end

API -> Validator: Validate exact candidate revision
activate Validator
Validator --> API: Validity and breaking-change status
deactivate Validator

break Required validation failed
  API --> Author: Validation errors; retain Draft
end

API -> Release: submit(candidate revision)
activate Release

Release -> Policy: calculateRisk(change scope, breaking, previous 30-day traffic)
activate Policy
Policy --> Release: Calculated tier and required stages
deactivate Policy

Release -> Release: Enter In Review; bind candidate revision
Release --> API: Release ID and risk tier
deactivate Release

API --> Author: Submission accepted
deactivate API

note over Reviewer,Release
  Tier 1: one Domain Approver.
  Tier 2: Domain Peer, then Workspace Owner.
  Tier 3: Domain Owner AND Compliance Officer.
  Maker is excluded from every approval role.
end note

loop While In Review; each review/override command
  Reviewer -> API: Approve / Reject / Increase risk tier
  activate API
  
  API -> Auth: Check scope and required review role
  activate Auth
  Auth --> API: Access decision
  deactivate Auth
  
  API -> Release: Check actor != maker, stage and candidate revision
  activate Release
  
  alt Unauthorized, maker, stale revision or invalid stage
    Release --> API: Reject command without counting approval
    API --> Reviewer: Review not accepted
  else Eligible reviewer
    alt Risk override
      API -> Release: overruleRiskUpward(newTier)
      alt newTier > effectiveTier
        Release -> Policy: Re-evaluate required approvals
        activate Policy
        Policy --> Release: New requirements
        deactivate Policy
        Release -> Evidence: Append override actor, tiers, reason and time
        activate Evidence
        Evidence --> Release: Recorded
        deactivate Evidence
      else Same or lower tier
        Release --> API: Reject override
      end
    else Reject
      API -> Release: recordReview(reject, reason)
      Release -> Evidence: Append immutable rejection for revision
      activate Evidence
      Evidence --> Release: Recorded
      deactivate Evidence
      Release -> Release: Return candidate to Draft
    else Approve
      API -> Release: recordReview(approve, reason)
      Release -> Evidence: Append immutable approval for revision
      activate Evidence
      Evidence --> Release: Recorded
      deactivate Evidence
      Release -> Policy: Check current stages / quorum
      activate Policy
      Policy --> Release: Satisfied or pending
      deactivate Policy
      opt All required approvals satisfied
        Release -> Release: Set Approved; freeze version
      end
    end
    Release --> API: Current governance status / command outcome
    API --> Reviewer: Review result
  end
  deactivate Release
  deactivate API
end

opt Approved and required validation remains satisfied
  Release -> Builder: build(approved exact revision)
  activate Release
  activate Builder
  Builder -> Builder: Bind graph, schemas, dependencies and library versions
  alt Build succeeds
    Builder -> Artifacts: Store immutable artifact, manifest and integrity metadata
    activate Artifacts
    Artifacts --> Builder: Stored
    deactivate Artifacts
    Builder --> Release: Artifact reference; eligible for delivery
  else Build fails
    Builder --> Release: Observable build error; no deliverable artifact
  end
  deactivate Builder
  deactivate Release
end

note over Release,Builder
  Approved does not mean Active.
  Approval reuse after upward override needs a policy/ADR decision.
  Old evidence never implicitly approves an edited revision.
end note
@enduml
